# Copy to `.deploy.env` (repo root, gitignored) and fill in your target machine's SSH address.
# Used by deploy/deploy.sh (and the Rider Run Configuration described in DEPLOY.md §9).
#
# NOTE: the value below is a leftover placeholder from the old reg.ru VPS. The current target is a
# different machine (Ubuntu 24.04 desktop, see DEPLOY.md intro) — replace both the user and the
# host/IP. It likely will NOT be `root@...`: see DEPLOY.md §9 for why the SSH user/sudo setup on this
# machine needs to be confirmed before the first automated deploy.
SSH_HOST=user@CHANGE_ME

# Only needed if the repo lives somewhere other than /opt/ezbook/app on the server
# REMOTE_DIR=/opt/ezbook/app
